  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1202.67 Fabric coating",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1202.67 \"Fabric coating\" means the coating of a textile substrate including, but not limited to, application by impregnation or saturation by the use of a knife, roll, or rotogravure coater to impart properties that are not initially present, such as strength, stability, water or acid repellency, or appearance. The term does not include fabric printing.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1200.html"
}
